# Config vs settings

Schema source of truth: `config.toml.example`.

## config.toml (bootstrap only)

Secrets and boot-time fields only:

- `[twitch]`: OAuth creds, channel, username, `owner` (bootstrap-only, not dashboard-editable)
- `[ai]`: `api_key` only
- `[aviationstack]`: `api_key` only
- `[web]`: `enabled`, `bind_addr`, `public_url`, `session_secret`

## settings.ron (runtime, dashboard-managed)

Everything else: permissions, channels, AI knobs, aviation toggles, schedules, web session TTL, etc. Lives under `$DATA_DIR/settings.ron`. Most changes apply live via `SettingsHandle`; backend/base_url/channel pointer changes require restart (UI shows badge).

## When adding a new knob

1. Secret or must exist before dashboard? → `config.toml.example` + loader
2. Runtime-tunable? → settings schema + dashboard card
3. Do not duplicate across both — legacy hoisted keys were migrated once via sentinels (`.ai_migrated_v2`, `.config_migrated_v3`, `.schedules_migrated_v3`); edits to migrated legacy keys are ignored
